Mass of uranyl absorbed:

\[
m_{\text{ads}}=(19.90-9.225)\ \mathrm{mg\,dm^{-3}}\times 0.2000\ \mathrm{dm^3}
\]

\[
m_{\text{ads}}=2.135\ \mathrm{mg}
\]

So the equilibrium adsorption capacity is

\[
q_e=\frac{2.135\ \mathrm{mg}}{5.000\times 10^{-3}\ \mathrm{g}}
=427.0\ \mathrm{mg\,g^{-1}}
\]

For the number of ions per pore:

\[
M(\mathrm{UO_2^{2+}})=238.03+2(16.00)=270.03\ \mathrm{g\,mol^{-1}}
\]

\[
n(\mathrm{UO_2^{2+}})=\frac{2.135\times 10^{-3}}{270.03}
=7.91\times 10^{-6}\ \mathrm{mol}
\]

The repeat unit of COF-9 is obtained from COF-8 plus conversion of three nitriles to amidoximes:

\[
\mathrm{COF\text{-}9}= \mathrm{C_{36}H_{27}N_9O_3}
\]

\[
M(\mathrm{COF\text{-}9})\approx 633.7\ \mathrm{g\,mol^{-1}}
\]

\[
n(\text{pores})=\frac{5.000\times 10^{-3}}{633.7}
=7.89\times 10^{-6}\ \mathrm{mol}
\]

Thus

\[
\frac{n(\mathrm{UO_2^{2+}})}{n(\text{pores})}\approx 1.00
\]

FINAL ANSWER: \(\boxed{q_e=427.0\ \mathrm{mg\,g^{-1}}}\); \(\boxed{1\ \mathrm{UO_2^{2+}}\text{ ion per COF-9 pore}}\).

Moles of methane released per day:

\[
n=\frac{PV}{RT}
=\frac{(101325\ \mathrm{Pa})(2.2\times 10^5\ \mathrm{m^3\,day^{-1}})}
{(8.314\ \mathrm{J\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}})(298\ \mathrm K)}
\]

\[
n \approx 9.0\times 10^6\ \mathrm{mol\,day^{-1}}
\]

Using \(\Delta_r H_{2000}\approx -781.9\ \mathrm{kJ\,mol^{-1}}\),

\[
E=n|\Delta_r H_{2000}|
=(9.0\times 10^6)(781.9\times 10^3)\ \mathrm{J\,day^{-1}}
\]

\[
E \approx 7.0\times 10^{12}\ \mathrm{J\,day^{-1}}
\]

FINAL ANSWER: \(\boxed{E \approx 7.0\times 10^{12}\ \mathrm{J\,day^{-1}}}\)

From 4.4, energy released per fission:

\[
\Delta E = 185.2\ \text{MeV}
\]

Total explosion energy:

\[
E_{\text{tot}} = 30\,000\ \text{ton TNT}\times 4.184\times 10^9\ \text{J ton}^{-1}
=1.2552\times 10^{14}\ \text{J}
\]

Energy per fission in joules:

\[
185.2\ \text{MeV}\times 10^6\ \frac{\text{eV}}{\text{MeV}}\times 1.602\times10^{-19}\ \frac{\text{J}}{\text{eV}}
=2.967\times10^{-11}\ \text{J}
\]

Thus

\[
T_N=\frac{1.2552\times10^{14}}{2.967\times10^{-11}}
=4.23\times10^{24}
\]

Only \(33\%\) of the \({}^{235}\mathrm U\) fissioned, so

\[
m=\frac{T_N}{0.33N_A}\times \frac{235.04\ \text{g mol}^{-1}}{0.90}
\]

\[
m=\frac{4.23\times10^{24}}{0.33(6.022\times10^{23})}
\times \frac{235.04}{0.90}\ \text{g}
\approx 5.56\times10^3\ \text{g}
=5.56\ \text{kg}
\]

FINAL ANSWER: \(T_N \approx 4.23\times10^{24}\) fissions; \(m \approx 5.6\ \text{kg}\) enriched uranium.

Take \(1.000\ \mathrm{g}\) of loaded material.

\[
m_{\text{cat}}=0.0380\ \mathrm{g},\qquad m_{\mathrm{C_3N_4}}=0.962\ \mathrm{g}
\]

Number of catalyst molecules:

\[
N=\frac{0.0380}{557.21}\times 6.022\times 10^{23}
=4.11\times 10^{19}
\]

Surface area of the \(\mathrm{C_3N_4}\):

\[
A=0.962\times 17.8\ \mathrm{m^2}
=17.12\ \mathrm{m^2}
=1.712\times 10^{19}\ \mathrm{nm^2}
\]

Thus

\[
N_{\text{cat}}=\frac{4.11\times 10^{19}}{1.712\times 10^{19}}
=2.40\ \mathrm{molecules\ nm^{-2}}
\]

FINAL ANSWER: \(\boxed{N_{\text{cat}}\approx 2.4\ \text{catalyst molecules nm}^{-2}}\)

For \(\mathrm{CO_2 \to CO}\), each CO molecule formed corresponds to \(2\) reacted electrons.

Using \(10.0\ \mathrm{mg}\) of \(\mathrm{C_3N_4}\) support and \(\omega_{\rm cat}=3.8\%\):

\[
m_{\rm cat}=0.0100\ \mathrm{g}\times \frac{0.038}{0.962}
=3.95\times 10^{-4}\ \mathrm{g}
\]

\[
n_{\rm cat}=\frac{3.95\times 10^{-4}}{557.21}
=7.09\times 10^{-7}\ \mathrm{mol}
\]

CO formed per hour:

\[
n_{\rm CO}=8\,n_{\rm cat}=5.67\times 10^{-6}\ \mathrm{mol\ h^{-1}}
\]

Reacted electrons per hour:

\[
n_{e^-}=2n_{\rm CO}=1.13\times 10^{-5}\ \mathrm{mol\ h^{-1}}
\]

Photons incident per hour:

\[
E_{\rm photon}=\frac{hc}{\lambda}
=\frac{(6.626\times 10^{-34})(2.998\times 10^8)}{390\times 10^{-9}}
=5.09\times 10^{-19}\ \mathrm{J}
\]

\[
n_{\rm photons}
=\frac{0.050\ \mathrm{J\,s^{-1}}\times 3600\ \mathrm{s}}{5.09\times 10^{-19}\ \mathrm{J}}\frac{1}{N_A}
=5.87\times 10^{-4}\ \mathrm{mol\ h^{-1}}
\]

Therefore,

\[
\varphi=\frac{n_{e^-}}{n_{\rm photons}}\times 100\%
=\frac{1.13\times 10^{-5}}{5.87\times 10^{-4}}\times 100\%
=1.93\%
\]

FINAL ANSWER: \(\boxed{\varphi \approx 1.9\%}\)
